{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A global minimum cut, over "},{"code":"directed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the least capacity of the edges between a nonempty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"proper vertex set and the rest, the set holding the first vertex as the source side; nil"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"below two vertices. By Nagamochi–Ibaraki (LEMON "},{"code":"NagamochiIbaraki","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; the same value as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"NetworkX "},{"code":"stoer_wagner","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost "},{"code":"stoer_wagner_min_cut","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", rustworkx "},{"code":"stoer_wagner_min_cut","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and igraph "},{"code":"mincut()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"): maximum adjacency orderings that contract every edge whose scanned"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connection is at least the best cut so far, so later phases run on smaller graphs. Which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minimum cut is returned when several exist is not specified, but the same input always"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gives the same cut. When the edges of positive capacity do not connect the graph, the cut"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of value zero whose source side is the first vertex’s component, with every crossing edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(all of capacity zero). Parallel capacities add; self-loops are ignored. "},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called once per non-loop edge, in position order, before any work (self-loops are never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asked). O(nm log n) in the worst case, far